  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An ideal gas is sealed in a cylinder with a sliding piston. When the piston is a length L from the bottom of the cylinder the total force of the gas particles on the piston is F<sub>total</sub> and the average force each individual particle imparts on the piston per collision is F<sub>particle</sub>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The piston length is slowly reduced to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{L}{2}\"></span> such that the temperature of the gas remains constant.</p>\n<p>What is true about the change in F<sub>total</sub> and the change in F<sub>particle</sub>?<br/><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
  },
